# Cache Strategy Decision

**Issue:** https://github.com/example/project/issues/42
**Date:** 2026-10-01T14:30:00Z
**Present:** Alice, Bob, Carol

## Decision

> **Redis Cluster**
>
> Best balance of performance and flexibility for our use case


## Requirements

| Requirement | Type | Active |
|---|---|---|
| P99 latency under 50ms | hard | ✅ |
| Stay within infrastructure budget | hard | ✅ |
| Supports distributed tracing | soft | ✅ |


## Items

| Item | Answer / Value |
|---|---|
| Expected peak traffic | Over 10k RPS |
| Multi-region deployment | Single region |
| Cache TTL | 300 seconds |
| Additional notes | Prioritize simplicity over flexibility |


## Design Options

### Redis Cluster

Managed Redis with read replicas

🟢 Possible · 1/2 hard · 1/1 soft

**Pros**
- Battle-tested
- Rich data structures

**Cons**
- Operational overhead

**Effects**
- [cost] Requires additional read replicas _(changes)_
- [performance] Connection pooling recommended _(note)_

### CDN Edge Cache

Cache at the edge with a CDN provider

❌ Eliminated · 2/2 hard · 0/1 soft

❌ **Failed:** Supports distributed tracing

**Pros**
- Zero operational overhead

**Cons**
- Limited invalidation control

